{"name":"Brown Teepee","hex":"#bca792","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"},{"term":"teepee","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cone-shaped tent traditionally used by many native peoples of the Great Plains of North America.","A conical formation of small flammable sticks leaning on each other, in roughly the shape of an Indian teepee, built over smaller tinder such as cotton or leaves."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Alternative form of TP (“to cover with toilet paper”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teepee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tipi","blocks":[{"text":"A tipi or tepee is a conical lodge tent that is distinguished from other conical tents by the smoke flaps at the top of the structure, and historically made of animal hides or pelts or, in more recent generations, of canvas stretched on a framework of wooden poles. The loanword came into English usage from the Dakota and Lakota languages."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Oglala_girl_in_front_of_a_tipi2.jpg/330px-Oglala_girl_in_front_of_a_tipi2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tipi"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown"}],"images":